 "In the reference model the FFN holds about two thirds of every block's parameters.": "",
 "Position-wise means: output row <0>t</0> depends only on input row <1>t</1>. There is no communication between rows inside the FFN.": "",
 "Llama-style models use a gated variant (SwiGLU) with three matrices (gate, up, down) instead of two.": "",
 "Because rows are independent, the FFN is trivially parallel across all tokens during prefill (<0>prefill</0>).": "",
