 "All three are ≈ identity for large positive x and ≈ {#} for large negative x. They differ near zero: ReLU has a sharp corner; GELU/SiLU are smooth and dip slightly below zero.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Probe</0>": "",
 "Without a non-linearity, stacking matrix multiplications collapses into one matrix. The activation is what makes depth useful.": "",
 "ReLU = max({#}, x) is simple and sparse; GELU and SiLU are smooth versions that let small negative values through.": "",
 "Modern LLMs usually use SiLU (as \"Swish\") inside a gated FFN.": "",
 "SiLU(x) = x · σ(x), where σ is the logistic sigmoid.": "",
 "GELU(x) ≈ {#}·x·({#} + tanh(√({#}/π)·(x + {#}.044715x³))) (the common tanh approximation).": "",
 "Which one is \"best\" is empirical; differences are small compared with architecture and data.": "",
