 "Like a soft lookup table with {#} slots per layer.": "",
 "It resembles attention (compare a query against keys, read out values), but the keys and values are <0>fixed weights</0> learned in training — not computed from the context.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Toy lookup</0>": "",
 "One way to read an FFN: each hidden unit is a <0>pattern detector</0> (a \"key\" = a column of W_up/W_gate) paired with an <1>output direction</1> (a \"value\" = a row of W_down).": "",
 "How strongly a pattern matches decides how much of its value is added to the residual stream.": "",
 "This is an <0>interpretive lens</0>, not a proven description of what every unit does.": "",
 "Research (e.g. \"Transformer Feed-Forward Layers Are Key-Value Memories\", Geva et al. {#}) found some units that respond to recognisable patterns; many units are polysemantic and messy.": "",
 "Facts such as \"Paris is in France\" are <0>often hypothesised</0> to be stored largely in FFN weights; evidence is suggestive, not settled.": "",
 "Do not confuse with the attention KV cache (<0>KV cache</0>), which stores per-token keys/values of the <1>context</1>.": "",
