 "Different tokens go to different experts. Experts are <0>not</0> hand-assigned topics; any specialisation emerges in training and is often subtler than \"this one does maths\".": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Router</0>": "",
 "An MoE layer replaces one big FFN with <0>E expert FFNs</0> plus a small <1>router</1>. Each token is sent to only its <2>top-k</2> experts (e.g. {#} of {#}).": "",
 "Total parameters grow with E, but compute per token only grows with k: more knowledge capacity at similar FLOPs.": "",
 "Training adds a <0>load-balancing</0> loss so tokens spread across experts instead of collapsing onto a few.": "",
 "Router: <0/> ([d_model × E]), softmax, keep top-k, renormalise those k weights; the output is the weighted sum of the chosen experts.": "",
 "All experts must still sit in memory, so MoE saves compute, not weight memory. Mixtral-style {#}×7B has ≈ {#} B total but ≈ {#} B active parameters.": "",
 "The reference model is <0>dense</0>; the MoE numbers here are an illustrative variant of it.": "",
